abstract: >-
  torch-dae is a reproducible PyTorch framework for integrating, verifying, and profiling
  checkpoint-specific audio embedding models. It separates the lightweight repository control
  plane from isolated model runtimes, records explicit Model Cards and runtime-verification
  evidence, exposes typed waveform, output, and embedding contracts, and supports repeatable
  device-specific profiling through Technical Cards with raw measurements. The repository also
  provides agent skills for controlled model onboarding and profiling. Research activities were
  mainly funded under the Ministerial Decree (DM) 118/2023, Mission 4, Component 1, Investment
  4.1 of the National Recovery and Resilience Plan (PNRR) – “PNRR Research” – CUP:
  E11I23000100001.
